{"id":"granicus-1-538","platform":"granicus","body":"City Council","name":"Special Park and Activities Commission Meeting","date":"2021-06-01","time":"","canceled":false,"agenda_url":"https://rollinghillsestatesca.granicus.com/AgendaViewer.php?view_id=1&clip_id=538","minutes_url":"https://rollinghillsestatesca.granicus.com/MinutesViewer.php?view_id=1&clip_id=538&doc_id=5a70dc45-feeb-11eb-81b1-0050569183fa","packet_url":"","clip_id":538,"view_id":1,"video_url":"https://rollinghillsestatesca.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=1&clip_id=538","transcript_url":"","mp4_url":"","mp3_url":"","agenda_text":"CITY OF\n\n  ROLLING HILLS ESTATES\n  4045 PALOS VERDES DRIVE NORTH • ROLLING HILLS ESTATES, CA 90274\n  TELEPHONE 310.377.1577 • FAX 310.377.4468\n  www.RollingHillsEstatesCa.gov\n\n  Special Meeting Agenda\n  PARK AND ACTIVITIES COMMISSION\n\nTuesday, June 1, 2021  6:00 PM  Teleconference\n\nNOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that a Special Meeting of the Park & Activities Commission of the City of\nRolling Hills Estates will be held on Tuesday, June 1, 2021 at 6:00 p.m. via Video Teleconference. The agenda for\nthe special meeting with the items to be discussed is set forth below.\n\n  Posted by the office of Community Services on Thursday, May 27, 2021\n  Pursuant to the Governor's Executive Order N-29-20, Park and Activities Commission Members will be\n  participating via teleconference.\n\n  - Commission meeting videos are live-streamed on the City’s website at www.rhe.city/agendas and\n  available for viewing thereafter. Commission meetings are recorded for minutes preparation purposes.\n\n  - Members of the public may listen to the meeting live by calling: (1-669-900-6833) from any phone,\n  Meeting ID: 939 0562 6430 , Meeting Password: 403923. (Please note you will not have the ability to\n  speak using the call-in option from a phone line.)\n\n  - Public correspondence may be emailed to Cynthia Morquecho, Community Services Supervisor at\n  cynthiam@rollinghillsestatesca.gov. Emails received before 5:00 p.m. the night of the meeting will be\n  forwarded to the Commission for their consideration and included as part of the record.\n\n  - Members of the public may comment online using eComment on the “Meeting Agendas, Minutes &\n  Videos” page of the City’s website (www.rhe.city/MeetingAgendas). Once the agenda is published, there\n  will be an “eComment” button next to the linked agenda under \"Upcoming Events\". Follow this link to\n  the City’s SpeakUp page. After you register, you may comment on any item on that particular agenda.\n  These comments can be seen by the public, will be considered by the Commission and become part of the\n  record.\n\n  - Members of the public who wish to speak during this meeting may join the Zoom meeting by accessing the\n  Zoom app from a computer (downloaded at Zoom.com) or tablet or phone (downloaded in the App Store),\n  by entering the following credentials: Meeting ID: 939 0562 6430, Meeting Password: 403923.\n\n  Members of the public who join the Zoom meeting will not have video, and may request to speak using the\n  following process: After joining the Zoom meeting, if you wish to speak, please select the \"raise hand\"\n  option at the lower portion of your screen. The Meeting Host will send you a chat message to identify\n  which item on the agenda you would like to speak on and will unmute your mic at the appropriate time.\n\n  Agenda reports and other disclosable public records relating to each agenda item are available on the\n  City's website under Meeting Agendas, Minutes & Videos at www.rhe.city.\n\nPARK AND ACTIVITIES COMMISSION  Page 1\n6/1/2021\nAmericans With Disabilities Act: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, if you require a disability-related\nmodification or accommodation to attend or participate in this meeting, including auxiliary aids or services, please call the\nCity Clerk's office at (310) 377-1577 at least 48 hours prior to the meeting.\n\fPark and Activities Commission  Special Meeting Agenda  June 1, 2021\n\n1.  CALL MEETING TO ORDER\n\n2.  SALUTE TO THE FLAG\n\n3.  ROLL CALL\n\n4.  APPROVAL OF MINUTES\n\n5.  AUDIENCE ITEMS NOT ON THE AGENDA\n\n6.  BUSINESS ITEMS\n\n  A.  NEW PROGRAM PROPOSAL- PLAYWELL LEGO SUMMER CAMP\n\n  Attachments: Staff Report\n\n  B.  RANCHVIEW REQUEST FOR BEAUTIFICATION FUNDS\n\n  Attachments: Staff Report\n\n  C.  ROLLINGWOOD TREE REPLACEMENT\n\n  Attachments: Staff Report\n\n  D.  2021 SUMMER MOVIE NIGHT PROGRAM\n\n  Attachments: Staff Report\n\n  E.  LEAGUE SHED REPLACEMENT REQUEST\n\n  Attachments: Staff Report\n\n  F.  PLAYGROUND STRUCTURE AT CHANDLER PARK UPDATE\n\n  Attachments: Staff Report\n\nPARK AND ACTIVITIES COMMISSION  Page 2\n6/1/2021\nAmericans With Disabilities Act: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, if you require a disability-related\nmodification or accommodation to attend or participate in this meeting, including auxiliary aids or services, please call the\nCity Clerk's office at (310) 377-1577 at least 48 hours prior to the meeting.\n\fPark and Activities Commission  Special Meeting Agenda  June 1, 2021\n\n7.  COMMISSION ITEMS (Verbal Report)\n\n  A.  ADOPT-A-PARK (VERBAL REPORT)\n\n  B.  MATTERS OF INTEREST (VERBAL REPORT)\n\n8.  STAFF ITEMS\n\n  A.  SPECIAL EVENT UPDATES (VERBAL REPORT)\n\n9.  MATTERS OF INFORMATION\n\n10.  FUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\n\n  A.  HIGHRIDGE PARK MURAL\n\n  B.  CONCERTS IN THE PARK\n\n11.  ADJOURNMENT\n  The next Park & Activities Commission will be held at 6:00 p.m. on June 21, 2021 at Ernie Howlett Park\n\nPARK AND ACTIVITIES COMMISSION  Page 3\n6/1/2021\nAmericans With Disabilities Act: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, if you require a disability-related\nmodification or accommodation to attend or participate in this meeting, including auxiliary aids or services, please call the\nCity Clerk's office at (310) 377-1577 at least 48 hours prior to the meeting.","minutes_text":"PK\u0003\u0004\u0